+| `getCapacityEvaluation` GET `/capacity-plans/{capacityPlanId}/evaluations/{evaluationId}` | 200; 404 `UNKNOWN_CAPACITY_EVALUATION` | common 400/401/403/503 | Read Accepted/Running/Completed/Failed without mutation; foreign scope 404. No replay. |
+
+## Lifecycle/fixture boundary that published wire errors depend on
+
+0190: Create Draft/null; capture from Draft or InReview appends immutable snapshot and sets InReview; sign-off only InReview against any same-plan snapshot, one decision per snapshot/role, no automatic plan Approved/Rejected even after all five roles approve. The sign-off state-conflict code is included in the published 2.0.0 contract. 0192: Capacity plan/scenario remain Draft in this bounded slice; evaluation alone may progress Accepted→Running→Completed/Failed under the **design-approved, not runtime-authorized** module-owned executor. The owner approved the startup+10-second scan, 30-second fenced lease and three-attempt **design for candidate preparation**, including the exact `DECISION.md` SHA-256 above; runtime implementation is still unauthorized. Terminal values come only from the exact fixture oracle `CAPACITY-EVAL-FIXTURE-192-01@1`; no live optimizer, supply-constraint source or Event Bus publisher. A Pending outbox event is written at terminal commit, no publisher delivery claim. Until Phase 1.5 and runtime DEV/VER authorization, terminal E4 acceptance remains HELD.
+
+The four approved scope limits are respected: exact tenant/LE test fixture for DEMAND with no producer endpoint; local trusted JWT actor/no Workflow; atomic Pending outbox/no publisher; Capacity fixture references/literal results only. A fixture PASS is not live DEMAND version/checksum or constraint producer validation. The 400/409/422/503 wire cases are included in the published amendment. Earlier executor/lifecycle/replay approvals were for candidate preparation; exact-hash consumer consent and publication were granted separately. Static candidate results alone do not prove runtime uptake.
+
