+## MOD-0192 executor design bound to exact approved decision hash
+
+The controlling design source is `docs/roadmap/plans/mod-0192-executor-exact-decisions-01/DECISION.md` SHA-256 `cfddf953a1a98107869417ef8afbcad5f578fcfde2a8cad8e1d2b6b05197cc5d`. The historical document itself remains unchanged and says PROPOSED; the later user message approved **that exact payload as design during candidate preparation**; subsequent exact-hash publication did not authorize runtime implementation.
+
+- A successful scoped claim of Accepted or expired Running atomically writes `status=Running`, version, a new monotonic fence, `leaseUntil`, and increments persisted `attempt` **in that claim**. Initial attempt is 0; successful claims are 1, 2, 3. Losing CAS is not an attempt; a claim followed by crash/expiry is.
+- Claim, renewal, expiry and terminal validity use Mongo primary **server UTC time**, not process/JWT/request time. A lease expires at `leaseUntil <= serverNow`. Each successful claim/renewal gives `serverNow + 30s`; target Mongo support for server-side time expressions is a Phase 1.5 technical gate, not assumed.
+- The executor signals after committed Accepted and scans on startup and every 10 seconds. While Running, a separate 10-second heartbeat renews only under current scope/status/version/fence and unexpired lease. Renewal does not increment attempt. A worker losing renewal does not attempt terminal persistence; any stale result is rejected by the fence.
+- Terminal commit requires scoped `Running`, current version/fence and `serverNow < leaseUntil`. A losing CAS writes no aggregate, slot, audit or outbox. Winning transaction atomically writes terminal Completed/Failed with `completedAt`, releases the active slot, and writes one terminal audit and one `capacity.evaluation.completed.v1` **Pending** outbox row. Event `occurredAt=completedAt`, original submit correlation and scenario-created causation. A unique terminal effect key prevents a second terminal event. Unknown terminal commit is resolved by reading scoped evaluation/event/audit before retry, never by blind second insert.
+- A third successful claim may complete normally while its lease is valid. If claim 3 crashes/expires, startup/scan first resolves any uncertain terminal commit, then performs a fenced atomic Failed terminal transaction **without claim 4 or fixture invocation 4**. Deterministic fixture rejection uses the same Failed path. Literal fixture oracle may run more than once after crashes; the guarantee is one durable terminal effect, not exactly-once computation.
+- Publisher remains absent; terminal outbox stays Pending. The executor is module-owned evaluation progress, not Event Bus delivery. Ten-second intervals and 30-second lease are configured intervals, not recovery SLA guarantees.
+
+The X01–X10 interruption/restart oracles in the approved `DECISION.md` are acceptance requirements for a later authorized isolated runtime DEV/VER; this static annex cannot establish those E4 outcomes.
+
