+2. Validate OpenAPI 3.1 schema, local refs and every positive/negative response example. For each of twelve rows exercise schema/model status/code/body/header/correlation positive and negative fixtures; a duplicate key and checksum mismatch fixture must detect incorrect behavior, not merely restate expected values.
+3. Compare 12 operation count, six S&OP/six Capacity, no new endpoint, no removed success/business status, no shared schema change except explicit new response components and `info.version`/annex pointer.
+4. Distinguish these schema/model checks from real HTTP/JWT/Mongo, producer uptake, consumer consent, guard, publication, pack promotion or rollout.
